{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["The reason for <b>And YHWH spoke to Moses in the wilderness of Sinai</b>: because Scripture mentioned (Numbers 3:1) \"on the day that YHWH spoke with Moses on Mount Sinai,\" it went back and stated that the appointment of the Levites' assignment was not on Mount Sinai, for the selection of the descendants of Aaron alone was on Mount Sinai on the day He commanded concerning the making of the Tabernacle, but the Levites were not commanded regarding their selection on Mount Sinai — only in the wilderness of Sinai, at the Tent of Meeting, like the command mentioned regarding the children of Israel. Now, the tribe of the Levites was not like the other tribes, for from a month old and upward they numbered only twenty-two thousand (Numbers 3:39), and from thirty years old all of them were eight thousand (Numbers 4:48), so they would not reach, from twenty years old and upward, even half the smallest tribe of Israel — and they had not yet carried the Ark, that the sanctity should consume them — and this is a wonder: how could His servants and His devout not be blessed by HaShem like the rest of all the people? And I think this supports what our Rabbis said (Tanhuma Va'era 6), that the tribe of Levi was not subjected to the bondage of Egypt's labor and crushing servitude. Now Israel, whom the Egyptians embittered with hard labor in order to diminish them — the Holy One, blessed be He, multiplied them against the decree of Egypt, as it says, \"and as they afflicted them, so they multiplied and so they spread\" (Exodus 1:12), and as is further said regarding the decree, \"if he is a son, put him to death\" — \"and the people multiplied and grew very mighty\" (ibid. v. 20), for the Holy One, blessed be He, was saying: let us see whose word will stand, Mine or theirs. But the tribe of Levi multiplied and increased in the manner of all the land, and did not rise above the other tribes. And perhaps this was because of the anger of the Patriarch against them: for Simeon, who is now numerous in population, was diminished upon entry into the land to twenty-two thousand, while Levi, who is the tribe of His devout, was not diminished by the plague."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:02:30.329795676Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}